          "heading": "Maro Itoje warns England not to sleepwalk into Eddie Jones's Japan test",
          "body": "Second-row Maro Itoje has warned England against complacency, saying they cannot \"sleepwalk\" into Saturday's test at Twickenham. \"Japan aren't most teams,\" Itoje said, so England must stay alive, impose their own game and keep their house in order. Itoje, who made his debut under Eddie Jones in 2016, expects his former coach to throw \"weird and wonderful\" tactics at them, and Jones has already hinted at unorthodox rugby."
