          "body": "The South African federation revealed 75 minutes before kick-off that the Springboks' starting and replacement front rows had been exchanged. Rugbyrama reports that Nations Championship rules, unlike those of the World Cup and Six Nations, did not forbid the change, which Rassie Erasmus had already used in the Rugby's Greatest Rivalry. In the build-up, France head coach Fabien Galthié had kept his Marcoussis camp closed to the press, Rugbyrama's Marc Duzan reported. France went on to win 21-19."
