          "kicker": "Squad age debate",
          "heading": "Stuart McCloskey says he couldn't care less about Ireland's ageing midfield",
          "body": "Ulster centre Stuart McCloskey, 34, was asked this week about the age of Ireland's midfield and was unbothered. He is one of four 30-somethings in a long-running four-way contest with Robbie Henshaw, Garry Ringrose and Bundee Aki. \"Honestly, I couldn't care less about the succession of what's going on after me,\" he told reporters in Abbotstown. The starting XV Andy Farrell picked against Argentina averaged 29.2 years, with eight players aged 30 or over."
