          "heading": "Townsend stresses individual responsibility after seven tries conceded to New Zealand",
          "body": "The problems against New Zealand were, in Scotland head coach Gregor Townsend's view, more about how the side gave the All Blacks chances inside its 22 than what the defence did. He framed it as individual responsibility, citing a player coming offside or not rolling away quickly. \"If you are giving those entries to the best teams in the world, they are looking to score over 50% of the time,\" Townsend said. Scotland conceded seven tries in the 21-43 defeat in Edinburgh last weekend."
